WEBVTT

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.240
(BEEPING)

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:44.880
(COIN DROPPING)

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.600
My name's Ralph, and I'm a bad guy.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.120
Let's see. I'm nine feet tall.
I weigh 643 pounds.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.280
Got a little bit of a temper on me.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.880
(GROWLING)

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.080
RALPH: My passion bubbles
very near the surface,

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:06.120
I guess, not gonna lie.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.160
Anyhoo, what else? Uh...

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.920
I'm a wrecker. I wreck things.
Professionally.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.560
I'm very good at what I do.
Probably the best I know.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:19.720
(YELLING)

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.720
The thing is, fixing
is the name of the game.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.480
Literally, Fix-It Felix, Jr.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.680
NICELANDERS:
Fix it, Felix!

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:27.920
(FELIX SPEAKING)

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.280
RALPH: So, yeah, naturally,

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.160
the guy with the name
Fix-It Felix is the good guy.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.080
He's nice enough as good guys go.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.080
Definitely fixes stuff really well.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:40.360
But, uh, if you've got a magic hammer
from your father,

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.960
how hard can it be?

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.320
If he was a regular contractor
carpenter guy,

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.920
I guarantee you would not be able

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.000
to fix the damage that I do as quickly.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.040
And when Felix does
a good job, he gets a medal.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:58.200
But are there medals for
wrecking stuff really well?

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:00.200
To that I say, "Ha!"

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.960
(GROWLS LOUDLY)

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.920
And, no, there aren't.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:05.960
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.160
Thirty years I've been doing this

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.080
and I've seen a lot of
other games come and go.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.280
Kind of sad. I think about
all those guys from Asteroids.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.800
Boom! Gone. Centipede?

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.720
Who knows where
that guy is, you know?

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.800
Look, a steady arcade gig
is nothing to sneeze at.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:23.960
I'm very lucky.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.480
It's just, I got to say,

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:30.080
it becomes kind of hard to love your job

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.440
when no one seems to
like you for doing it.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.640
All clear! The arcade is closed!

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.320
Shoryuken!

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:44.440
Whoo! What a day! You want to
head to Tappers, Ken?

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.000
If you're buying, buddy.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:51.120
FELIX: Quitting time!

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.840
RALPH: I don't know.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.480
Maybe I wouldn't be feeling this way

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.560
if things were different after work.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.080
But it is what it is.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.240
Good job, everyone!

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.800
RALPH: Felix and the Nicelanders

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.760
go hang out in their homes

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.400
which he's just fixed,
and everyone, you know...

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.320
They go to their homes, I go to mine

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.240
which happens to be a dump.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.040
And when I say "a dump,"

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:29.440
I don't mean like a shabby place.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.040
I mean an actual dump,

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.280
where the garbage goes

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.680
and a bunch of bricks
and smashed building parts...

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.360
That's what I call home.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:42.600
I guess I can't bellyache too much.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.320
I got my bricks, I got my stump.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.400
It looks uncomfortable.
It's actually fine. I'm good.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:04:00.600
But if I'm really honest with myself...

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:05.440
I see Felix up there
getting patted on the back,

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.640
people are giving him pie
and thanking him

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:12.800
and so happy to see him all the time.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.080
Sometimes I think...

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:20.320
Man, it sure must be nice
being the good guy.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.080
(ALL CLAPPING)

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:25.720
CLYDE: Nice share, Ralph.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:27.200
As fellow bad guys,

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.680
we've all felt what you're feeling

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:30.200
and we've come to terms with it.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.720
-Really?
-ZANGIEF: Right here.

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:33.800
I am Zangief. I am bad guy.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.120
-ALL: Hi, Zangief!
-Hi, Zangief.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.240
I relate to you, Ralph.
When I hit bottom,

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.880
I was crushing man's skull

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.680
like sparrow egg between my thighs.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:44.920
(ALL CHUCKLING)

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.960
And I think, "Why do you have
to be so bad, Zangief?

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.480
"Why can't you be more like good guy?"

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:53.160
Then I have moment of clarity.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.200
If Zangief is good guy,

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:57.240
who'll crush man's skull

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:59.520
like sparrow's egg between thighs?

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:01.800
And I say, "Zangief, you are bad guy,

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:05.280
"but this does not mean
you are 'bad' guy."

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.080
(GRUNTS IN APPROVAL)

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.360
Right. I'm sorry. You lost me there.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:12.960
-Zombie! Bad guy!
-ALL: Hi, Zombie.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.400
Hi, Zombie.

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:17.920
Zangief saying
labels not make you happy.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.240
Good! Bad!

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.480
(GROWLS)

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:23.760
You must love you.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.160
-Yeah! Inside here!
-Yes.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:29.320
Okay. All right, I get you.
Watch out. It's dripping.

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:30.440
Question, Ralph.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:33.120
We've been asking you
to Bad-Anon for years now

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:36.280
and tonight you finally show up.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:38.120
-Why is that?
-I don't know.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:39.600
I just felt like coming.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:44.000
I suppose it has
something to do with the fact that...

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.320
Well, today is the 30th
anniversary of my game.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.320
Well, happy anniversary, Ralph.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:50.640
Thanks, Satan.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.280
Uh, it's Sateen, actually.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.560
Got it. But here's the thing.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:56.680
(SIGHS)

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.040
I don't want to be the bad guy anymore.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:01.600
(ALL EXCLAIMING)

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.480
You can't mess with
the program, Ralph.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:08.200
You're not going Turbo, are you?

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:11.680
Turbo? No, I'm not going Turbo!
Come on, guys!

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:14.680
Is it Turbo to want a friend?
Or a medal?

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:16.720
Or a piece of pie every once in a while?

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:18.520
Is it Turbo to want more out of life?

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:19.960
Yes!

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:21.960
Ralph, Ralph, we get it.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:24.000
But we can't change who we are.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:25.360
And the sooner you accept that,

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:28.760
the better off your game
and your life will be.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.040
Hey. One game at a time, Ralph.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:34.720
Let's close out with
the Bad Guy Affirmation.

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:42.280
ALL: I'm bad, and that's good.

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:46.160
I will never be good, and that's not bad.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.520
There's no one I'd rather be than me.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.520
CLYDE: Okay, gang,
see you next week.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:53.600
M. BISON: Listen, I can't do
snacks next week.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.200
Hang in there, Ralph.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:57.720
CLYDE: Hey, Zombie,
don't forget your hatchets.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:58.880
There you go.

